_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Propagate alias-symlink removal failures before copying.**

If removal fails, `fs::copy` follows the remaining symlink and can overwrite the alias target—the corruption this branch intends to prevent.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 if dest_path.is_symlink() {
-    let _ = fs::remove_file(&dest_path);
+    fs::remove_file(&dest_path).map_err(|e| {
+        io::Error::new(
+            e.kind(),
+            format!("removing destination alias {}: {e}", dest_path.display()),
+        )
+    })?;
 }
```
</details>

